# Copy to .env.local for development, or paste into Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
# Never commit .env.local. Nothing here is a secret; every value that is one is named, not given.

# --- The commerce backend -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. The storefront reads Medusa during the server render,
# so neither of these is ever inlined into the browser bundle.
#
# Both may be left empty. A storefront deployed ahead of its backend builds and serves the
# editorial catalogue with every bottle reading "arriving soon" -- see CONFIGURED in
# src/lib/medusa.ts. Set MEDUSA_URL to a backend that cannot be reached and the build fails
# loudly instead, which is the correct behaviour for an outage.
MEDUSA_URL=
# Admin -> Settings -> Publishable API Keys. Scopes the store API to a sales channel. Public in
# the sense that it identifies rather than authorises, but there is no reason to ship it to the
# browser, so it stays server-side.
MEDUSA_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Payments -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Razorpay *public* key id (rzp_test_... or rzp_live_...), from the same account as the
# backend's RAZORPAY_KEY_ID in medusa/.env. NEVER the secret: NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the
# browser bundle. Empty is a valid state -- the checkout button then says payments are being
# switched on rather than opening an empty till.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# --- Canonical origin -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every absolute URL the metadata layer emits: og:url, the sitemap, the Sitemap: line in
# robots.txt. Set it per environment, with no trailing slash. Unset falls back to the intended
# production domain rather than localhost, so a preview deploy still emits share cards that
# point somewhere real.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://swasthvica.com
